# RoboCarl (AI brief)

Prefer this over codebase exploration. Open specific files only when editing them. **Update this rule** when levels, systems, or folder layout change.

## Game
2D URP portrait puzzle, playfield **9×19.5** (`AspectRatioCamera`). Player does **not** control Carl — Carl walks to closest **LOS-visible** oil/battery; player uses **draggable** or **button** walls, plus **power buttons** for devices. Energy drains ~100s idle / ~25s walking (same pool); oil drains with walk. Energy 0 → lose. WinLine → MainMenu.

## Levels
| Level | Path | Notes |
|------:|------|-------|
| 1 | `LevelSession=1` → `SampleScene` | Scene: floors, ground Spring, WinLine, Carl. Spawns from `Resources/DefaultLevelSpawns` |
| 2 | `LevelSession=2` → **same** `SampleScene` | Full floor; keep WinLine. Keeps right ground battery, spikes, `DraggableWall` (yellow ↔ drag arrows). Adds left battery+spring, one-way platform, `ButtonWall` gate, platform oil/spring/battery |
| 3 | `LevelSession=3` → **same** `SampleScene` | Full floor; Carl between two `ButtonWall` gates + center `LinkedWallButton` (wires, slides both). Fans at screen ends (`±4.1`) with energy/oil in front. Left fan mounted `PowerButton`; right fan wired button above. |

- Menu levels 1–3 only (`MainMenuController`). Play Mode starts on `MainMenu`.
- **`Level2.unity` is unused** — not the L2 runtime path.
- `LevelSpawnConfig`: pickups, walls, buttonWalls, platforms, springs, spikes. Prefer editing those assets over `.unity` YAML. Fans/power buttons spawned from `Level3Layout` (need live refs for wires).

## L1 anchors (SampleScene)
- Floor Y **-3.84** (thickness **0.08**, black). Carl start ~(0, **-3.25**) — ⅓ up screen with camera at y=0.
- Ground spring ~(1, -3.975), size 1.2×0.35 — **top flush with floor top**.
- WinLine Y = `WinLine.DefaultHeight` (**1.31**), full width.
- Spring tops must be walkable from the surface Carl is on (flush or within step-up ~20% of Carl height). Spawn position is the spring **center**, not the top.
- **Spring side-stuck:** Flush springs are solid boxes; after Carl stops against one (e.g. blocked by a wall), physics can keep him on a **side** contact (`normal.y ≈ 0`) so the pad never fires and feels like a wall. `SpringPad` also mounts when Carl is grounded with feet at the pad top; `TryStepUp` allows ~0 flush lifts. Keep both if changing spring/step logic.
- One-way platforms: thin lighter deck + corner supports; `PlatformEffector2D`. Solid for LOS (elevated pickups hidden from below). Ignored by start `SnapFeetToGround` so Carl doesn't spawn on a deck above him.
- Spikes: side hit → 25° knockback away (vx preserved; ground-brake disabled during knockback) + 1s grounded decision lock after settle; top hit → MainMenu. Not treated as ground; LOS ignores them.
- Fans (`PoweredFan` / `IPowerable`): sprites `Resources/Props/Prop_FanHousing` + `Prop_FanBlades`. Powered by `PowerButton` (multi-target; wire and/or mounted). On → blades spin + wind streaks; hum while on-camera. Pushes Carl + oil/battery with distance falloff.
- `LinkedWallButton`: one press triggers `ButtonWall.TryTriggerToggle()` on each linked door from its own current position; per-door buttons still work alone.

